docs {
  A1 Exam Day, end to end, on A1 Modelltest 1 (catalogue number 9):
  telc Start Deutsch 1, Übungstest 1.

  WHAT THIS CHECKS
  The same journey as A2 Level, on A1's own rows: the picker offers the
  paper as A1, Hören runs first for 20 minutes with one recording and one
  play per Teil, Lesen und Schreiben runs second for 45 minutes and serves
  the A1 shapes (two letters in Lesen Teil 1, a Bar/Kreditkarte choice in
  the form), the key decides every closed answer, a misspelt form answer
  waits for the examiner, and the result ends PASSED at 52 of 60.

  BEFORE YOU START
  1. Rebuild the fixture (it adds the A1 student and seat):
         node scripts/seed-b2-bruno-fixture.mjs
     It must print "A1 papers  9" and database ep-misty-sea, never
     ep-wandering-hall.
  2. Run the API against that database:  npm run start:testdb
  3. Center Auth / 03 Login, so {{accessToken}} is set.

  ORDER AND TIMING
  Run in seq order. 04 creates a sitting that opens three minutes later:
  run 05 and 06 inside those three minutes, then WAIT until the opensAt in
  04's response before 07.

  HÖREN PLAYS
  The recordings live in R2 under a1-mt-hoeren/a1-mt-1-hoeren/ (492, 231
  and 292 seconds). A1 Hören is all closed answers (a/b/c, richtig/falsch),
  so the answer key decides the whole of it at submit.

  RE-RUNNING
  02 claims the A1 seat. A second run is 409 — re-run the fixture script.
}
